{"tool_name":"oufti","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"oufti","home":"http://www.oufti.org/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Oufti is an open-source software package designed for analysis of microscopy data.","addition_date":"2018-08-28T13:20:10Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:59:01Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:oufti","credit":[{"email":"christine.jacobs-wagner@yale.edu","name":"Christine Jacobs-Wagner","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.oufti.org/tutorial.htm"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"}]}],"name":"Oufti","operating_system":["Mac","Windows"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.1111/mmi.13264","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 John Wiley & Sons Ltd.With the realization that bacteria display phenotypic variability among cells and exhibit complex subcellular organization critical for cellular function and behavior, microscopy has re-emerged as a primary tool in bacterial research during the last decade. However, the bottleneck in today's single-cell studies is quantitative image analysis of cells and fluorescent signals. Here, we address current limitations through the development of Oufti, a stand-alone, open-source software package for automated measurements of microbial cells and fluorescence signals from microscopy images. Oufti provides computational solutions for tracking touching cells in confluent samples, handles various cell morphologies, offers algorithms for quantitative analysis of both diffraction and non-diffraction-limited fluorescence signals and is scalable for high-throughput analysis of massive datasets, all with subpixel precision. All functionalities are integrated in a single package. The graphical user interface, which includes interactive modules for segmentation, image analysis and post-processing analysis, makes the software broadly accessible to users irrespective of their computational skills.","authors":[{"name":"Campos M."},{"name":"Elf J."},{"name":"Irnov I."},{"name":"Jacobs-Wagner C."},{"name":"Paintdakhi A."},{"name":"Parry B."},{"name":"Surovtsev I."}],"citationCount":147,"date":"2016-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Molecular Microbiology","title":"Oufti: An integrated software package for high-accuracy, high-throughput quantitative microscopy analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC4752901","pmid":"26538279","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Light microscopy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3385"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Oufti","home":"https://bio.tools/oufti","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Oufti is an open-source software package designed for analysis of microscopy data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:oufti/app/www.oufti.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":254,"citations":[{"count":10,"year":"2016"},{"count":12,"year":"2026"},{"count":20,"year":"2018"},{"count":20,"year":"2020"},{"count":21,"year":"2023"},{"count":22,"year":"2022"},{"count":24,"year":"2019"},{"count":25,"year":"2017"},{"count":26,"year":"2024"},{"count":31,"year":"2025"},{"count":43,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1111/mmi.13264","pmcid":"PMC4752901","pmid":"26538279","ref_count":10,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1969"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":3,"year":"2014"}],"title":"Oufti: an integrated software package for high-accuracy, high-throughput quantitative microscopy analysis.","year":2015}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/oufti","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"markdown","processed":"","summary":"","value":"Oufti (previously named MicrobeTracker) is a MATLAB application / suite of tools for analysing fluorescent spots inside microbes. MicrobeTracker can identify cell outlines and fluorescent foci, and generate plots and statistics based on positions and intensity (kymographs, histograms etc.) The MATLAB code is easy to modify and extend to add additional plots and statistics: see e.g. [Lesterlin et al. (2014)](http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24362571).\r\n\r\nThe Outfi Forum is [quite active](https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/ouftiinfo). \r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-05-25T22:52:55+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2014-12-08T16:55:58+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[{"target_id":4476,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"c600078e-427b-4d57-a51f-a2d2b95dc10c","url":"/taxonomy/term/4476"},{"target_id":4643,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"c33a8a10-83f2-4cd4-844a-e2baa1e7f217","url":"/taxonomy/term/4643"},{"target_id":4644,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"a5791f2d-05c2-4d80-9b11-94dba834718e","url":"/taxonomy/term/4644"}],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":nul